<title>FINLAND: AAMULEHTI SOARS TO RECORD-HIGHS ON MERGER.</title>
<headline>AAMULEHTI SOARS TO RECORD-HIGHS ON MERGER.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Finnish media group Aamulehti-yhtyma Oy soared to an all-time high 195.00 markka following news that it planned to merge with commercial television company MTV Oy, brokers said.</p>
<p>At 1205/0905 GMT, Aamulehti traded at 195.00 markka, up 40.50 markka or 23 percent. Turnover was fair for Aamulehti at little over three million markka.</p>
<p>Brokers said the merger would secure Aamulehti's place as a major player in the Finnish media business.</p>
<p>&quot;The new company looks very attractive -- it will be the first listed electronic media company on the Helsinki bourse,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>&quot;This will create serious competition for Sanoma (Oy),&quot; said another.</p>
<p>--Veera Heinonen, Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 240,</p>
